(iv) date, time and location of the accident;
(v) the name(s) and address(es) of witness(es);
(vi) the name(s) and address(es) of injured
person(s) and type of injuries sustained;
(vii) whereabouts of injured person(s);
(viii) damages to vehicle(s) and/or property;
(ix) circumstances surrounding the cause of the
accident;
(b) where necessary, despatch injured person(s) to a
Government Medical Institution for attention;
(c) warn the driver(s) of “intended prosecution”
according to law;
(d) In the case of the officer away from the Station:
(i) record the information at paragraph (a) in
his Pocket Diary;
(ii) mark the point of impact and position of
vehicle(s);
(iii) cause the vehicle(s) to be removed from the
roadway, in order to avoid unnecessary
obstruction;
(iv) refer the person(s) involved to the Police
Station in the District in which the accident
occurred;
(v) report the facts of the accident to the Second
Division Officer-in-charge of the Station
District in which the accident occurred;
(e) In the case of the officer at Station:
(i) record the information at paragraph (a) in
the Station Diary;
(ii) inform the Second Division Officer-in-
charge of the Station/Charge Room/Traffic
Section of the report.
