(ii) record the following information: 
In relation to the Driving Permit:
the number;
date issued; 
expiry date; and
class of vehicle(s) the holder is entitled to
drive;
In relation to the Certificate of Insurance:
the number; 
date commenced; 
expiry date;
name of insurer; and
name of the insured.
In relation to the Licence:
the licence number; and the year for which
paid;
(c) visit the “scene” the same day of the report and:
(i) secure any evidence that may assist in the
investigation of the accident;
(ii) despatch injured person(s) to a Medical
Institution;
(iii) interview the driver(s) and witnesses;
(iv) take the following measurements:
(1) the width of the road; 
(2) the point of impact which must be pointed
out by the parties involved, e.g., driver(s) or
pedestrian, to the nearest side of the road-
way. When the parties concerned are not in
agreement with the point of impact
indicated by each other, record any
measurement or point of impact indicated
by each driver;
(3) any other measurements that are relevant
to the accident including skid marks,
brakes or tyre impressions;
