(d) make an official record of the following:
(i) debris, which may assist in determining an
accurate point of impact;
(ii) the direction in which the vehicles, persons or
animals were travelling;
(iii) any other evidence which may assist in identi-
fying the cause of the accident;
(iv) record the extent of the damages to vehicle(s) or
property or injury to persons or animals;
(e) record statements from the driver(s) and witnesses.
In the case of a very serious accident in addition to the duties
from (a) to (e) above, he shall do the following:
(f) have the scene photographed, including the
vehicle(s) and property if necessary;
(g) cause the vehicles to be removed to the nearest
Police Station and prevent persons other than the
Inspecting Engineer from interfering with them;
(h) have the vehicle inspected by an Inspecting
Engineer from the Licensing Authority, within four
(4) days of the accident;
(i) return the vehicle to the owner, as soon as it has
been inspected and photographed.
In the case of a Fatal Accident in addition to the duties from (f)
to (i) above he shall do the following:
(j) cover the body of the victim;
(k) request the services of the District Medical Officer to
view and authorise the removal of the body;
(l) make efforts to have the body identified;
(m) secure any valuables found on the body of the victim
and lodge them with the Property Manager at
Station;
